Z||000000||rockcrawl||11-30-2000||08:20 PM||||I just got a Corvette power steering rack to use on my Testarossa project. It will be an easy swap. The body of the rack is the same length, and it will bolt to the Fiero with minor mods. It uses the same non-symetrical double "D" shaft with the same diameter. Now on to my question. The corvette uses a standard ratio of 2.25 turns and a performance ratio of 2 turns. The Fieros are 3.5 and 3 turns. Is the 2.25 turn Vette rack going to be too quick? Of course steering effort is not my concern, but rather responsiveness. I'm afraid the car will be too twitchy. The tires will be 40 series on 17x9 rims.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
