Z||000010||mrfixit58||12-01-2000||02:32 PM||||Rockcrawl,<P>I've been searching the bone yards for a suitable power rack and the one that look like they would fit are all rear steer cars. Geo, Sunfires, etc. Is the Corvette a front steer or a rear steer? <P>Front steer means that (like the Fiero) the tie rod ends fasten to the spindle in front of the front wheels. Rear steer means (of couse) that the tie rods fasten behind the front wheels. If you put a front steer rack on a rear steer car then when you turn the wheel left, the car turns right. Might be rough to get used to.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||4
